## Coding standards (PHPCS / PHPCBF)

Each contrib module ships its own `phpcs.xml`. **Always detect and use it** — do not hardcode `--standard=Drupal` alone, as modules like `ai` add `DrupalPractice` too.

The example below uses the default site's webroot. When working against a
different site, substitute that site's Webroot from the table above.

**Always run via `ddev exec`** — the container PHP version matches CI; host PHP may not.

```bash
ddev exec php vendor/bin/phpcs --standard={{DRUPAL_WEBROOT}}/modules/contrib/<module>/phpcs.xml <relative-path>
ddev exec php vendor/bin/phpcbf --standard={{DRUPAL_WEBROOT}}/modules/contrib/<module>/phpcs.xml <relative-path>
```

Pass paths **relative to the Drupal root** — `ddev exec` runs from `/var/www/html`. Use the **`/drupal-coding-standards`** skill which handles root detection, config discovery, and path conversion automatically.

If a module has no `phpcs.xml`, fall back to `--standard=Drupal --extensions=php,module,inc,install,test,profile,theme,info,engine,yml`.

Walk **up** from the target file toward the project root to find the nearest `phpcs.xml` — submodules (e.g. `ai_agents/modules/ai_agents_views/`) inherit the parent module's config.

