## Contribution toolchain

Two CLI tools are required and both are installed:

| Tool | Command | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| drupalorg-cli | `drupalorg` | Issue/MR lifecycle (show, diff, checkout, push) |
| GitLab CLI | `glab` | Pipeline status, inline threads, MR ops |

**`glab` must always be prefixed with `GITLAB_HOST=git.drupalcode.org`** when targeting the Drupal GitLab instance. It is authenticated — no token setup needed.

`drupalorg-cli` also runs as an MCP server (configured in `.mcp.json` for Claude Code or `.codex/config.toml` for Codex) exposing
read-only tools like `issue_show`, `mr_list`, `mr_diff`, `mr_status`,
`gitlab_issue_show`. These work for classic (non-migrated) Drupal.org issues.
For **migrated** issues (GitLab work items), any tool that resolves a project
from `nid` alone (`mr_list`, `mr_status`, `mr_files`, `issue_get_fork`,
`issue_show`) errors or returns empty/garbage data — the classic Drupal.org
REST lookup can't map a migrated nid to its project. Only `gitlab_issue_show`
(pass the full work-item URL) works correctly there. Prefer the Bash `drupalorg`
and `glab` commands documented above for migrated-issue workflows until this is
fixed upstream.

