## Skills and agents

Skills live under `<skills-root>`. Shared role procedures are installed in `.drupal-contrib/agents/`; the installer also generates each client's native agent definitions.

### Agents
- `drupal-issue-agent` — full lifecycle: MR review (Path A) and new issue implementation (Path B)
- `drupal-e2e-tester` — dedicated test phase: PHPUnit via ddev + Playwright browser e2e; report-only, never edits code
- `drupal-issue-catchup` — sync after time away: fetches new comments/threads, updates record, briefs human
- `drupal-repo-setup` — sub-agent for git/module setup: clone, remote, checkout, worktree

### Entry point skills
- `drupal-issue-start` — **PRIMARY ENTRY POINT**: load/create issue record, fetch live context, present report, wait for direction
- `issue-record-update` — append timestamped session log to `issues/<nid>/README.md` (writes directly, no confirmation)
- `issue-record-screenshot` — capture a browser screenshot into `issues/<nid>/screenshots/` using the connected browser session
- `drupalorg-comment-format` — draft and save comments to `issues/<nid>/comments/` (HTML for Drupal.org, GFM for GitLab)

### Other key skills
- `drupal-issue-reroll` — rebase a branch on latest upstream, run checks, force-push
- `drupal-gitlab-inline-comments` — fetch MR inline threads and issue notes
- `drupal-coding-standards` — PHPCS/PHPCBF via ddev with automatic module config detection
- `drupalorg-cli` — reference stub; run `drupalorg skill:get drupalorg-cli` before using any `drupalorg` command; pulled from `mglaman/drupalorg-cli` at setup time (not part of this package — update with `npx skills update`)
- `ddev-expert` — ddev environment management, troubleshooting, container commands
- `drupal-automated-testing` — writing/modifying PHPUnit tests: test type selection, attributes, DDEV env vars
- `playwright-cli` — browser automation for the e2e test phase; pulled from `microsoft/playwright-cli` at setup time (not part of this package — update with `npx skills update`)
